ation against your course material.\n\nReport an issue\n1:53 PM\n\nI am stuck; explain simply and give me a small hint.\n\n1:53 PM\n\nHint – add the probabilities\n\nIn the unequal‑probability example there are two red counters each with probability \n0.30\n0.30 and one green counter with probability \n0.40\n0.40. To find the chance of drawing a red counter, simply add the probabilities of the two red outcomes.\n\nYour turn: Calculate the probability of drawing a red counter\n\nNo source reference attached. Verify this explanation against your course material.\n\nReport an issue\nMAKE FLASHCARDS\nSave these gaps for spaced repetition\nCREATE QUIZ\nGenerate a short check on this skill\nOPEN KNOWLEDGE MAP\nSee this concept in context\nCONTINUE PATH\nBuild a guided plan from here\nSAVE AS NOTE\nCapture this tutor step in notes\nLEARNING REVIEW\nReview connected study work\n1:53 PM\nTUTOR\nNUDGE\nTEACH\nCHECK ME\nDRILL\nOpen ContextHub","errors":[]}
